            <div xml:id="d203">

                <pb facs="0160" n="152" xml:id="pg152"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1386: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-01-24T18:00:00-05:00">January 24, 1939—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7. Your telegram of January 20, No. 8, 3 p.m. There is no objection to your plan
                    for the Commission to meet in Panama upon the arrival there of Dr. Zúñiga
                    Montúfar.</p>
                <p>Careful consideration will be given to the suggestion contained in the second
                    sentence of the last paragraph of your telegram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
